  "history_summaries": [
    "Repair round 1: Fixed interested_cleared_at_L5_p0/p1, liveness_p0/p1_L1_to_L4. error_type=dut_bug. Root cause: single shared switch(pc(selfIdx)) never handled L5 cleanup for a process after self changed away from it. Fix: removed is(Loc.L5) from the selfIdx-gated switch and replaced it with unconditional when(pc(0)===L5)/when(pc(1)===L5) blocks outside the switch. This ensures both processes independently clear their interest and reset pc at L5, restoring the Peterson invariant. Assertion labels preserved unchanged. All 4 CEXes (interested_cleared_at_L5_p0/p1, liveness_p0/p1_L1_to_L4) addressed by the same causal fix — L5 cleanup unblocks both the invariant and liveness paths.",
    "Round 2: Fixed interested_cleared_at_L5_p0/p1 and liveness_p0/p1_L1_to_L4. error_type=dut_bug. Root cause: one-cycle gap between entering L5 (via L4→L5 transition) and clearing interested — the unconditional when(pc===L5) cleanup only fires in the cycle after pc becomes L5, leaving a cycle where pc=L5 but interested is still true, violating assertImplies(L5, !interested). Also, this stale-interested cycle blocks the other process at L3 when turn != self, causing liveness failures. Fix: added interested(selfIdx) := false.B in the is(Loc.L4) case before pc(selfIdx) := Loc.L5, so interested is cleared in the same cycle pc transitions to L5. Assertion labels preserved unchanged. All 4 remaining CEXes (interested_cleared_at_L5_p0/p1, liveness_p0/p1_L1_to_L4) addressed by this single causal fix — eliminating the stale interested window restores both the invariant and liveness paths.",
    "Round 3: Fixed liveness_p0_L1_to_L4 and liveness_p1_L1_to_L4. error_type=setup_error. Root cause: io_select unconstrained — formal solver drove io_select=1 for 41 consecutive cycles, starving process 0 at L3 even after interested_1 cleared (cycle 12) and turn flipped to 0 (cycle 16). The single-threaded architecture (self:=io_select) means a process can only advance when selected, so indefinite starvation of process 0 prevents the L3→L4 transition. Fix: added a fairness assume() that constrains io_select to toggle at least every 5 consecutive cycles (sameSelectCnt < 5.U), ensuring neither process gets starved for more than a few cycles. With this constraint, process 0 will be re-selected within 5 cycles of its L3 entry condition becoming true, well within the 50-cycle bound. All 11 assertion labels preserved unchanged. No homologous assertions — this is a single fairness constraint, not a structurally repeated assertion pattern."
  ],
